 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? Not at all. Many adults learn new languages in their fifties. The best time was ten years ago, but second best is now. That's okay. Start with simple phrases and build your confidence. Listening is the easiest part, and many people learn mostly by osmosis. Both are great choices. Portuguese will open doors in Europe, and Greek is beautiful and easy to start with. The basics are fairly simple. Greetings, personal information, numbers, and food. A basic tense, like present simple, is usually the first thing to master.",
